WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.680
Look at the chair you're sitting in right now.

00:01.840 --> 00:03.620
Like, take a take in and actually feel it.

00:03.720 --> 00:05.000
Yeah, just really notice it.

00:05.040 --> 00:06.240
It feels solid, right?

00:06.460 --> 00:08.940
It feels stable, feels well-finished.

00:09.120 --> 00:11.400
And usually, when we navigate the world,

00:11.520 --> 00:14.200
we carry this deeply ingrained expectation

00:14.200 --> 00:15.700
of that kind of solidity.

00:15.840 --> 00:16.600
We absolutely do.

00:16.640 --> 00:18.880
We look at a mountain or a skyscraper,

00:19.040 --> 00:21.080
an institution, or even ourselves,

00:21.180 --> 00:23.400
and we think, you know, that is a thing.

00:23.500 --> 00:24.580
That is a permanent noun.

00:24.680 --> 00:25.720
Right, a finished object.

00:25.940 --> 00:26.340
Exactly.

00:26.880 --> 00:28.780
But the document we are unpacking today

00:28.780 --> 00:30.780
argues that your chair is an illusion.

00:31.240 --> 00:32.180
A total illusion.

00:32.480 --> 00:34.120
It is not a static object at all.

00:34.120 --> 00:36.940
It is actually a desperate, ongoing,

00:37.360 --> 00:38.960
physical process of repair.

00:39.500 --> 00:41.820
It is vibrating with the energetic cost

00:41.820 --> 00:43.300
of maintaining its own boundaries.

00:43.560 --> 00:46.080
And the moment it stops fighting that entropic battle,

00:46.220 --> 00:47.620
it just collapses.

00:47.960 --> 00:50.440
Today, we are going to completely dismantle

00:50.440 --> 00:51.940
how you look at reality.

00:52.500 --> 00:55.140
We are pulling you away from a comfortable world of things

00:55.140 --> 00:57.560
and plunging you into a universe of processes,

00:57.560 --> 01:00.600
histories, and just relentless maintenance.

01:01.060 --> 01:02.220
So welcome to another Deep Dive.

01:02.560 --> 01:04.040
I am so excited for this one.

01:04.480 --> 01:06.400
We are fundamentally shifting the question

01:06.400 --> 01:07.940
we ask about the universe today.

01:08.160 --> 01:09.480
Yeah, it's a massive shift.

01:09.720 --> 01:12.020
We are moving away from looking at our surroundings

01:12.020 --> 01:15.780
and asking, uh, what is this?

01:16.040 --> 01:17.360
We are going to start asking,

01:17.760 --> 01:19.140
how is this being maintained?

01:19.820 --> 01:21.920
And what happens to the future

01:21.920 --> 01:23.740
when that maintenance fails?

01:23.740 --> 01:25.080
To guide us through this,

01:25.200 --> 01:27.960
we are pulling from this incredibly dense,

01:28.320 --> 01:31.540
highly technical, like 70-plus page document.

01:31.820 --> 01:33.000
It is a brick of a text.

01:33.100 --> 01:33.680
It really is.

01:33.800 --> 01:36.440
It is titled theflictionbriefing.pdf.

01:36.700 --> 01:39.080
The date on it is June 2026.

01:39.260 --> 01:39.500
Right.

01:39.620 --> 01:41.140
Authored by an independent researcher.

01:41.440 --> 01:43.880
Operating under the GitHub handle Standard Galactic.

01:44.360 --> 01:45.980
And let me be clear for everyone listening,

01:46.560 --> 01:48.240
this is not a narrow academic paper

01:48.240 --> 01:50.500
focused on one tiny sliver of science.

01:50.620 --> 01:51.080
Not at all.

01:51.080 --> 01:52.440
This is a comprehensive briefing

01:52.440 --> 01:54.340
on something called the Flyxion Research Program,

01:54.620 --> 01:56.420
and it is attempting something monumental.

01:56.840 --> 01:58.060
Monumental is the right word.

01:58.140 --> 01:59.920
It is laying out a unified theory

01:59.920 --> 02:01.580
that spans theoretical physics,

02:02.060 --> 02:02.940
artificial intelligence,

02:03.380 --> 02:04.180
software engineering,

02:04.580 --> 02:05.460
cognitive architecture,

02:05.460 --> 02:08.320
and literally the macroeconomic rise and fall

02:08.320 --> 02:09.440
of human civilizations.

02:10.060 --> 02:11.300
The sheer scope of it

02:11.300 --> 02:13.540
is just what makes it so worth dissecting.

02:13.660 --> 02:13.800
Yeah.

02:14.020 --> 02:15.540
The author is trying to articulate

02:15.540 --> 02:17.780
what they call a process-native perspective.

02:17.780 --> 02:21.180
It is a unifying language

02:21.180 --> 02:23.540
for how complex systems survive

02:23.540 --> 02:25.060
in an entropic universe.

02:25.320 --> 02:27.280
And while the math inside this briefing

02:27.280 --> 02:28.400
is highly complex,

02:28.940 --> 02:30.400
the underlying mental models

02:30.400 --> 02:32.260
are things you can immediately apply

02:32.260 --> 02:33.060
to your career.

02:33.520 --> 02:35.060
You can apply it to your understanding

02:35.060 --> 02:36.260
of modern technology

02:36.260 --> 02:39.220
and just how you view your own daily life.

02:39.300 --> 02:40.480
Which makes it so practical,

02:40.820 --> 02:41.940
despite the heavy math.

02:42.020 --> 02:42.480
Exactly.

02:42.480 --> 02:44.480
So the mission for this deep dive

02:44.480 --> 02:45.960
is to act as your shortcut

02:45.960 --> 02:48.320
through this dense, unified theory.

02:48.780 --> 02:50.200
We are going to extract

02:50.200 --> 02:51.560
the most critical insights

02:51.560 --> 02:53.460
so you do not have to wade through

02:53.460 --> 02:55.060
the differential equations yourself.

02:55.220 --> 02:56.720
I mean, unless you really want to.

02:56.840 --> 02:57.640
Right, exactly.

02:57.980 --> 02:59.260
Okay, let's unpack this.

02:59.660 --> 03:00.940
Before we get anywhere near

03:00.940 --> 03:02.780
the theoretical physics of the cosmos

03:02.780 --> 03:03.920
or the code bases

03:03.920 --> 03:05.120
for artificial intelligence,

03:05.340 --> 03:06.520
we have to understand

03:06.520 --> 03:07.800
the fundamental frustration

03:07.800 --> 03:10.440
that birthed this entire research program.

03:10.560 --> 03:11.260
The starting point.

03:11.260 --> 03:12.640
Yeah, it starts with a concept

03:12.640 --> 03:14.300
the author calls the noun problem.

03:14.680 --> 03:15.340
Let's start there.

03:15.720 --> 03:17.400
So the noun problem

03:17.400 --> 03:19.160
is this cognitive bias.

03:19.600 --> 03:21.600
It is deeply hardwired

03:21.600 --> 03:22.760
into human perception

03:22.760 --> 03:23.660
and human language.

03:23.960 --> 03:25.340
We just love nouns.

03:25.520 --> 03:26.400
We really do.

03:26.540 --> 03:27.400
We use them because

03:27.400 --> 03:28.540
they are highly efficient

03:28.540 --> 03:29.900
compressions of reality.

03:30.220 --> 03:31.240
When we talk about

03:31.240 --> 03:32.680
like the Roman Empire

03:32.680 --> 03:34.300
or a scientific theory

03:34.300 --> 03:35.580
or a piece of software,

03:35.880 --> 03:37.380
we frame them as static,

03:37.560 --> 03:38.740
immutable objects.

03:38.860 --> 03:39.100
Right.

03:39.100 --> 03:40.460
But the Flyxion framework

03:40.460 --> 03:42.520
argues that this linguistic convenience

03:42.520 --> 03:44.320
fundamentally blinds us

03:44.320 --> 03:45.140
to how the universe

03:45.140 --> 03:46.180
actually operates.

03:46.320 --> 03:47.100
How so?

03:47.260 --> 03:48.200
Well, none of those examples

03:48.200 --> 03:49.260
are static objects.

03:49.400 --> 03:51.060
They are all localized,

03:51.320 --> 03:52.300
ongoing processes

03:52.300 --> 03:53.480
of continuous repair.

03:53.860 --> 03:54.620
I mean, I can see

03:54.620 --> 03:55.560
why we do it, though.

03:56.200 --> 03:57.260
If I had to describe

03:57.260 --> 03:57.940
the Roman Empire

03:57.940 --> 03:58.800
not as a noun,

03:58.940 --> 03:59.840
but as this daily

03:59.840 --> 04:01.020
exhausting process

04:01.020 --> 04:01.860
of border maintenance

04:01.860 --> 04:02.860
and crop management

04:02.860 --> 04:04.240
and political assassinations

04:04.240 --> 04:06.200
and infrastructural repair,

04:06.300 --> 04:07.060
I would never be able

04:07.060 --> 04:07.780
to finish a sentence.

04:07.780 --> 04:08.320
Exactly.

04:08.640 --> 04:10.160
Nouns are incredibly useful.

04:10.240 --> 04:10.980
Yeah, they save time.

04:11.340 --> 04:11.920
They are useful

04:11.920 --> 04:13.260
for casual communication,

04:13.640 --> 04:14.860
but they are disastrous

04:14.860 --> 04:15.900
for formal modeling.

04:16.860 --> 04:17.680
The author's critique

04:17.680 --> 04:19.460
is that our most successful,

04:19.920 --> 04:20.760
rigorous frameworks

04:20.760 --> 04:22.220
like classical mechanics

04:22.220 --> 04:24.060
or traditional computer science

04:24.060 --> 04:25.240
or classical logic,

04:25.940 --> 04:27.300
they have all internalized

04:27.300 --> 04:28.240
this noun bias.

04:28.420 --> 04:28.980
Oh, I see.

04:29.180 --> 04:30.480
They treat their objects of study

04:30.480 --> 04:32.100
as primitive and static.

04:32.560 --> 04:33.840
They build their foundations

04:33.840 --> 04:34.880
on static states

04:34.880 --> 04:36.040
and fixed propositions

04:36.040 --> 04:37.080
and solid objects.

04:37.080 --> 04:37.980
But if reality

04:37.980 --> 04:39.140
isn't actually static,

04:39.280 --> 04:40.060
that's a problem.

04:40.420 --> 04:40.640
Right.

04:41.000 --> 04:41.520
When you build

04:41.520 --> 04:43.080
your entire scientific worldview

04:43.080 --> 04:44.100
on static nouns,

04:44.300 --> 04:45.160
you accumulate

04:45.160 --> 04:46.240
a massive residue

04:46.240 --> 04:46.940
of problems

04:46.940 --> 04:48.180
that your paradigm

04:48.180 --> 04:49.620
simply cannot solve.

04:49.740 --> 04:50.640
What kind of problems

04:50.640 --> 04:51.580
are we talking about here?

04:51.720 --> 04:53.260
Questions of dynamic persistence,

04:54.040 --> 04:56.060
like how do complex belief systems

04:56.060 --> 04:57.840
actually revise themselves

04:57.840 --> 04:58.660
when confronted

04:58.660 --> 04:59.480
with new evidence?

04:59.640 --> 05:00.220
Oh, interesting.

05:00.360 --> 05:01.720
Or how do software systems

05:01.720 --> 05:02.560
actually tolerate

05:02.560 --> 05:03.460
cascading faults

05:03.460 --> 05:04.200
in the real world?

05:04.580 --> 05:05.860
Why do seemingly stable

05:05.860 --> 05:06.860
human civilizations

05:06.860 --> 05:08.200
just suddenly collapse?

05:08.580 --> 05:09.500
You cannot answer

05:09.500 --> 05:10.280
a question about

05:10.280 --> 05:11.420
structural collapse

05:11.420 --> 05:13.720
if your fundamental worldview

05:13.720 --> 05:15.000
treats the structure

05:15.000 --> 05:16.220
as an immortal noun.

05:16.460 --> 05:17.500
You literally don't have

05:17.500 --> 05:18.340
the math for it.

05:18.580 --> 05:20.740
So, to fix this blind spot,

05:21.200 --> 05:22.280
the Flyxion program

05:22.280 --> 05:23.080
demands that we

05:23.080 --> 05:24.080
completely invert

05:24.080 --> 05:24.680
our thinking.

05:24.840 --> 05:25.900
Total paradigm shift.

05:25.960 --> 05:26.560
They outline

05:26.560 --> 05:27.520
a new foundation

05:27.520 --> 05:28.760
through what they call

05:28.760 --> 05:30.340
the five core commitments.

05:30.840 --> 05:31.680
These are essentially

05:31.680 --> 05:32.360
the physical

05:32.360 --> 05:33.900
and philosophical laws

05:33.900 --> 05:34.780
of this process

05:34.780 --> 05:35.700
native universe.

05:35.820 --> 05:36.620
The rules of the game.

05:37.020 --> 05:37.920
Let's walk through them.

05:38.420 --> 05:39.420
The first commitment

05:39.420 --> 05:41.140
is history before state.

05:41.520 --> 05:42.540
The premise here

05:42.540 --> 05:44.080
is that how a system

05:44.080 --> 05:44.920
arrived at its

05:44.920 --> 05:45.740
current configuration

05:45.740 --> 05:47.640
is vastly more important

05:47.640 --> 05:48.580
and more fundamental

05:48.580 --> 05:50.300
than the configuration itself.

05:50.660 --> 05:51.520
Standard computing

05:51.520 --> 05:52.640
is the ultimate example

05:52.640 --> 05:53.220
of the old

05:53.220 --> 05:54.400
noun-based thinking here.

05:54.540 --> 05:54.980
How so?

05:55.420 --> 05:56.360
Well, standard software

05:56.360 --> 05:57.260
just looks at the current

05:57.260 --> 05:58.280
state of a machine's memory.

05:58.640 --> 05:59.200
It registers

05:59.200 --> 06:00.100
that a variable

06:00.100 --> 06:01.120
is currently equal

06:01.120 --> 06:02.320
to five, right?

06:02.820 --> 06:03.880
It does not care

06:03.880 --> 06:05.040
what sequence of operations

06:05.040 --> 06:05.980
led to that number.

06:06.100 --> 06:07.000
It just sees the five.

06:07.280 --> 06:07.500
Right.

06:07.700 --> 06:08.760
It treats the current state

06:08.760 --> 06:09.820
as the absolute truth.

06:10.660 --> 06:11.920
The process native framework

06:11.920 --> 06:12.860
argues that a state

06:12.860 --> 06:13.920
is merely a highly

06:13.920 --> 06:15.000
compressed projection

06:15.000 --> 06:15.620
of history.

06:15.720 --> 06:15.940
Okay.

06:16.120 --> 06:16.960
And the information

06:16.960 --> 06:17.760
you throw away

06:17.760 --> 06:18.840
when you compress a history

06:18.840 --> 06:19.940
into a single state,

06:20.440 --> 06:21.180
that cannot be

06:21.180 --> 06:21.920
safely ignored.

06:22.200 --> 06:22.400
Okay.

06:22.500 --> 06:23.360
I am going to push back

06:23.360 --> 06:23.840
on this a bit

06:23.840 --> 06:25.680
because practically speaking,

06:25.680 --> 06:26.900
this feels really

06:26.900 --> 06:27.740
counterintuitive.

06:28.160 --> 06:28.720
Let's hear it.

06:28.880 --> 06:30.080
Think about my bank account.

06:30.840 --> 06:31.980
Isn't the current state

06:31.980 --> 06:32.940
of my checking account

06:32.940 --> 06:34.460
what actually dictates

06:34.460 --> 06:35.220
my reality?

06:35.580 --> 06:35.980
Go on.

06:36.100 --> 06:37.520
If I walk into a grocery store

06:37.520 --> 06:38.760
and my balance is $100,

06:39.460 --> 06:41.380
that state is the single

06:41.380 --> 06:42.360
determining factor

06:42.360 --> 06:44.060
of whether I can buy food.

06:44.380 --> 06:46.280
The history of how I spent

06:46.280 --> 06:47.420
my money over the last

06:47.420 --> 06:47.980
five years,

06:48.060 --> 06:49.280
like all the coffee I bought,

06:49.420 --> 06:50.120
the rent I paid,

06:50.640 --> 06:52.540
that history doesn't matter

06:52.540 --> 06:53.420
at the checkout counter.

06:53.640 --> 06:54.760
The state is the only

06:54.760 --> 06:55.840
functional reality.

06:56.040 --> 06:57.880
That is the exact scenario

06:57.880 --> 06:58.940
the author uses

06:58.940 --> 07:00.180
to explain what they call

07:00.180 --> 07:01.340
the provenance problem.

07:01.500 --> 07:01.840
Really?

07:02.100 --> 07:02.440
Yes.

07:03.060 --> 07:04.480
You are looking at a system

07:04.480 --> 07:06.160
operating under completely

07:06.160 --> 07:08.200
frictionless normal conditions.

07:08.320 --> 07:08.860
Okay, fair.

07:09.180 --> 07:09.440
Yes.

07:09.680 --> 07:10.640
When everything is working

07:10.640 --> 07:11.080
perfectly,

07:11.280 --> 07:12.320
your $100 balance

07:12.320 --> 07:13.600
is a highly efficient,

07:14.040 --> 07:14.840
useful compression

07:14.840 --> 07:15.900
of your financial history.

07:16.260 --> 07:17.940
It allows you to buy groceries

07:17.940 --> 07:19.100
without dragging

07:19.100 --> 07:20.040
a physical ledger

07:20.040 --> 07:22.100
of 10,000 past transactions

07:22.100 --> 07:23.280
to the cash register.

07:23.600 --> 07:24.600
Which would be exhausting.

07:24.960 --> 07:25.360
Exactly.

07:25.880 --> 07:26.900
But what happens

07:26.900 --> 07:28.180
if an anomaly occurs?

07:29.080 --> 07:30.040
Imagine you open

07:30.040 --> 07:30.780
your banking app

07:30.780 --> 07:31.660
in the checkout line

07:31.660 --> 07:33.080
and your balance

07:33.080 --> 07:34.440
says negative $500.

07:35.020 --> 07:35.780
Oh, man.

07:35.900 --> 07:36.800
I would freeze.

07:37.020 --> 07:38.240
I wouldn't know what to do.

07:38.320 --> 07:38.980
And why wouldn't

07:38.980 --> 07:39.740
you know what to do?

07:40.720 --> 07:41.660
Because the state,

07:41.820 --> 07:42.620
the static noun

07:42.620 --> 07:43.660
of negative $500,

07:44.380 --> 07:45.560
contains absolutely

07:45.560 --> 07:46.640
zero information

07:46.640 --> 07:47.660
about why it exists.

07:47.840 --> 07:48.960
That makes total sense.

07:49.200 --> 07:50.380
The state cannot explain

07:50.380 --> 07:51.160
its own existence.

07:51.160 --> 07:53.200
It is functionally useless

07:53.200 --> 07:54.920
for resolving the crisis.

07:55.380 --> 07:56.460
In order to survive

07:56.460 --> 07:57.060
this anomaly,

07:57.480 --> 07:59.020
what is the very first thing

07:59.020 --> 07:59.780
you have to request

07:59.780 --> 08:00.380
from the bank?

08:00.640 --> 08:01.800
I need the transaction history.

08:02.180 --> 08:03.560
I need the itemized ledger.

08:03.780 --> 08:04.340
I have to see

08:04.340 --> 08:05.840
if there was a fraudulent charge

08:05.840 --> 08:07.240
or like a double-billed

08:07.240 --> 08:08.160
utility payment.

08:08.300 --> 08:09.200
I need to trace it back.

08:09.460 --> 08:10.360
You need the provenance.

08:10.580 --> 08:11.300
You need the history

08:11.300 --> 08:12.660
to perform a repair.

08:12.820 --> 08:13.200
Wow.

08:13.400 --> 08:14.520
This proves that history

08:14.520 --> 08:16.200
was always the fundamental reality.

08:16.880 --> 08:17.660
The state was just

08:17.660 --> 08:18.260
a convenient,

08:18.520 --> 08:19.260
lossy projection

08:19.260 --> 08:20.660
that only functioned smoothly

08:20.660 --> 08:21.860
as long as nothing

08:21.860 --> 08:22.780
in the system broke.

08:22.860 --> 08:24.040
And things always break.

08:24.320 --> 08:24.720
Exactly.

08:25.260 --> 08:27.160
When complex systems break

08:27.160 --> 08:29.280
and in an entropic universe,

08:29.680 --> 08:30.880
everything eventually breaks,

08:31.180 --> 08:32.420
you cannot reconstruct

08:32.420 --> 08:33.540
the history from the state.

08:33.760 --> 08:34.960
You need the history

08:34.960 --> 08:35.620
to survive.

08:35.880 --> 08:36.100
Okay.

08:36.260 --> 08:37.440
That clarifies it completely.

08:37.820 --> 08:39.080
The state is a luxury.

08:39.600 --> 08:41.180
We only get to enjoy states

08:41.180 --> 08:42.900
when the underlying processes

08:42.900 --> 08:44.320
are functioning flawlessly.

08:44.740 --> 08:45.900
Once they falter,

08:45.900 --> 08:47.080
we are forced back

08:47.080 --> 08:48.300
into the reality of history.

08:48.940 --> 08:49.440
Beautifully put.

08:49.440 --> 08:50.160
That takes us

08:50.160 --> 08:51.720
to the second core commitment,

08:52.320 --> 08:53.820
distinction before object.

08:54.240 --> 08:55.460
We usually assume objects

08:55.460 --> 08:56.580
just exist out there

08:56.580 --> 08:57.580
in the void, right?

08:57.780 --> 08:59.000
Like a rock is a rock.

08:59.120 --> 09:00.080
A planet is a planet.

09:00.400 --> 09:01.420
And our brains

09:01.420 --> 09:02.300
or our telescopes

09:02.300 --> 09:04.080
just passively observe them.

09:04.340 --> 09:05.840
But the framework says no.

09:06.280 --> 09:06.980
It argues that

09:06.980 --> 09:07.980
maintaining a boundary

09:07.980 --> 09:08.860
between an inside

09:08.860 --> 09:09.760
and an outside,

09:10.200 --> 09:10.880
between one thing

09:10.880 --> 09:11.620
and another thing,

09:11.880 --> 09:13.480
requires an active expenditure

09:13.480 --> 09:14.880
of energy and resources.

09:14.880 --> 09:15.880
Positive expenditure.

09:16.280 --> 09:16.400
Right.

09:16.400 --> 09:17.940
The capacity to maintain

09:17.940 --> 09:18.520
a distinction

09:18.520 --> 09:20.040
is physically prior

09:20.040 --> 09:20.880
to the identification

09:20.880 --> 09:21.760
of an object.

09:22.280 --> 09:23.440
Objects do not exist

09:23.440 --> 09:24.340
as primitive facts

09:24.340 --> 09:24.960
of the universe.

09:25.580 --> 09:26.280
They are the temporary

09:26.280 --> 09:27.240
stable products

09:27.240 --> 09:28.540
of an ongoing process

09:28.540 --> 09:29.720
of distinction maintenance.

09:29.860 --> 09:29.960
Okay.

09:30.060 --> 09:31.620
Think about a biological cell.

09:31.740 --> 09:32.400
Great example.

09:32.740 --> 09:33.900
A cell only exists

09:33.900 --> 09:34.500
as an object

09:34.500 --> 09:35.400
because it is

09:35.400 --> 09:36.900
constantly burning ATP.

09:36.900 --> 09:38.540
It is constantly

09:38.540 --> 09:39.680
utilizing energy

09:39.680 --> 09:41.000
to pump ions

09:41.000 --> 09:42.280
across its membrane,

09:42.940 --> 09:44.020
maintaining the distinction

09:44.020 --> 09:45.100
between the internal

09:45.100 --> 09:45.920
cellular fluid

09:45.920 --> 09:47.420
and the external environment.

09:47.620 --> 09:48.180
It is working

09:48.180 --> 09:49.220
to stay distinct.

09:49.480 --> 09:50.940
If it stops spending energy

09:50.940 --> 09:51.840
on that distinction,

09:52.240 --> 09:53.180
if it dies,

09:53.400 --> 09:54.620
the boundary dissolves,

09:54.740 --> 09:55.760
the chemicals mix.

09:56.020 --> 09:57.360
It is no longer an object.

09:57.520 --> 09:58.440
It just becomes part

09:58.440 --> 09:59.520
of the background noise.

09:59.760 --> 10:00.920
Which is a beautiful setup

10:00.920 --> 10:01.880
for the third commitment,

10:02.220 --> 10:02.900
reachability

10:02.900 --> 10:04.340
before representation.

10:04.560 --> 10:05.320
This one is tricky.

10:05.540 --> 10:05.940
It is.

10:05.940 --> 10:07.380
In traditional science

10:07.380 --> 10:08.080
and epistemology,

10:08.240 --> 10:09.020
we judge the value

10:09.020 --> 10:09.600
of a model

10:09.600 --> 10:11.220
based on how accurately

10:11.220 --> 10:12.040
it represents

10:12.040 --> 10:14.280
a static external reality.

10:14.440 --> 10:14.840
Like how good

10:14.840 --> 10:15.720
of a map it is.

10:15.820 --> 10:16.060
Right.

10:16.740 --> 10:17.740
But the Flyxion program

10:17.740 --> 10:19.300
states that the primary value

10:19.300 --> 10:20.180
of any representation

10:20.180 --> 10:21.940
is whether it preserves

10:21.940 --> 10:23.100
your future possibilities

10:23.100 --> 10:23.760
for action.

10:24.180 --> 10:24.980
Reachability means

10:24.980 --> 10:26.120
keeping your options open.

10:26.280 --> 10:26.520
Yes.

10:27.260 --> 10:28.240
Representational fidelity

10:28.240 --> 10:29.380
and the preservation

10:29.380 --> 10:30.300
of reachability

10:30.300 --> 10:31.500
are two entirely

10:31.500 --> 10:32.220
different metrics

10:32.220 --> 10:33.820
and they frequently conflict.

10:34.100 --> 10:34.780
Give me an example

10:34.780 --> 10:35.260
of that.

10:35.260 --> 10:35.700
Okay.

10:35.940 --> 10:36.800
You can possess

10:36.800 --> 10:38.840
a flawlessly accurate

10:38.840 --> 10:40.040
map of a maze.

10:40.640 --> 10:41.480
But if following

10:41.480 --> 10:42.760
the most efficient path

10:42.760 --> 10:43.480
on that map

10:43.480 --> 10:44.560
leads you through

10:44.560 --> 10:45.540
a one-way door

10:45.540 --> 10:46.720
that locks behind you,

10:47.040 --> 10:47.620
trapping you

10:47.620 --> 10:48.680
in a dead end,

10:48.820 --> 10:49.600
Oh, wow.

10:49.840 --> 10:50.900
that representation

10:50.900 --> 10:52.160
has destroyed

10:52.160 --> 10:52.960
your reachability.

10:53.100 --> 10:53.300
Hmm.

10:53.300 --> 10:54.260
The framework

10:54.260 --> 10:55.460
prioritizes maps

10:55.460 --> 10:56.600
that keep you in regions

10:56.600 --> 10:57.420
where you can still

10:57.420 --> 10:58.160
make choices.

10:58.400 --> 10:59.060
Even if the map

10:59.060 --> 11:00.200
is a little less accurate,

11:00.320 --> 11:01.440
as long as it keeps you safe.

11:01.540 --> 11:01.760
Exactly.

11:01.760 --> 11:03.140
And when you inevitably

11:03.140 --> 11:04.480
make a wrong choice,

11:04.620 --> 11:05.720
you rely on the fourth

11:05.720 --> 11:06.180
commitment.

11:06.720 --> 11:08.200
Repair before correctness.

11:08.580 --> 11:09.820
This goes back to the

11:09.820 --> 11:10.560
maintenance nightmare

11:10.560 --> 11:11.340
of reality.

11:11.580 --> 11:12.480
Everything degrades.

11:12.740 --> 11:13.160
Everything.

11:13.720 --> 11:14.700
If you design a software

11:14.700 --> 11:15.740
system or a legal

11:15.740 --> 11:17.380
framework or a biological

11:17.380 --> 11:18.660
ecosystem to achieve

11:18.660 --> 11:20.080
and to sit in a final,

11:20.260 --> 11:21.640
perfect, correct state,

11:22.180 --> 11:22.880
you have engineered

11:22.880 --> 11:23.840
a brittle system

11:23.840 --> 11:24.860
that will shatter upon

11:24.860 --> 11:26.040
contact with a changing

11:26.040 --> 11:26.540
environment.

11:26.540 --> 11:27.920
The systems that persist

11:27.920 --> 11:28.800
over deep time

11:28.800 --> 11:29.680
do not survive

11:29.680 --> 11:30.080
because they are

11:30.080 --> 11:30.720
perfectly correct.

11:31.280 --> 11:32.200
They survive because

11:32.200 --> 11:33.860
they possess robust,

11:34.160 --> 11:34.940
layered mechanisms

11:34.940 --> 11:36.080
for continuous repair.

11:36.580 --> 11:36.980
And finally,

11:37.080 --> 11:37.620
the fifth commitment,

11:37.860 --> 11:38.720
which is deeply tied

11:38.720 --> 11:40.160
to artificial intelligence,

11:40.780 --> 11:42.120
admissibility before prediction.

11:42.480 --> 11:43.160
We are going to dig

11:43.160 --> 11:44.180
heavily into this later.

11:44.280 --> 11:45.220
We definitely are.

11:45.420 --> 11:46.840
But the baseline idea

11:46.840 --> 11:47.900
is that optimizing

11:47.900 --> 11:49.460
for one highly predicted

11:49.460 --> 11:50.740
outcome is incredibly

11:50.740 --> 11:51.200
