19:55.960 --> 19:56.500
the partition,

19:56.820 --> 19:57.800
the distinction collapses.

19:58.380 --> 19:59.340
The two separate things

19:59.340 --> 20:00.660
blur back into a single,

20:01.060 --> 20:02.300
undifferentiated state.

20:02.740 --> 20:03.500
And when a system

20:03.500 --> 20:04.580
lacks the resources

20:04.580 --> 20:06.080
to maintain the distinctions

20:06.080 --> 20:07.360
necessary to navigate

20:07.360 --> 20:08.040
its environment,

20:08.520 --> 20:09.380
it suffers from what

20:09.380 --> 20:10.200
the other terms

20:10.200 --> 20:11.680
an ontological deficit.

20:11.860 --> 20:12.820
An ontological deficit

20:12.820 --> 20:13.920
is far more dangerous

20:13.920 --> 20:15.040
than simple ignorance.

20:15.420 --> 20:16.380
If you are ignorant,

20:16.760 --> 20:18.300
you possess the correct categories,

20:18.420 --> 20:19.400
you just haven't collected

20:19.400 --> 20:20.300
enough data yet.

20:20.300 --> 20:21.460
You have empty boxes

20:21.460 --> 20:22.400
waiting to be filled.

20:22.520 --> 20:23.200
That makes sense.

20:23.560 --> 20:24.700
But an ontological deficit

20:24.700 --> 20:25.660
means your boxes

20:25.660 --> 20:26.380
are fundamentally

20:26.380 --> 20:27.260
the wrong shape.

20:27.840 --> 20:28.840
Your very categories

20:28.840 --> 20:30.500
are structurally insufficient

20:30.500 --> 20:32.320
to capture the causal mechanics

20:32.320 --> 20:33.280
of the reality

20:33.280 --> 20:34.340
you are operating within.

20:35.220 --> 20:36.040
Gathering more data

20:36.040 --> 20:36.760
won't help you.

20:37.040 --> 20:37.660
Let's map this

20:37.660 --> 20:40.200
to a concrete mechanical example

20:40.200 --> 20:41.580
so people can really picture this.

20:42.080 --> 20:43.460
Imagine trying to play

20:43.460 --> 20:45.320
a massively complex

20:45.320 --> 20:47.920
modern 4K video game,

20:48.100 --> 20:49.360
but you are playing it

20:49.360 --> 20:50.920
on a 1950s

20:50.920 --> 20:52.820
black and white television set.

20:52.820 --> 20:54.060
Oh, that's a great analogy.

20:54.380 --> 20:55.140
In this game,

20:55.280 --> 20:56.300
your survival depends

20:56.300 --> 20:57.540
on a specific mechanic.

20:58.080 --> 20:59.000
You have to run

20:59.000 --> 21:00.160
