21:39.560 --> 21:40.320
You have to repair

21:40.320 --> 21:41.340
the apparatus itself.

21:41.720 --> 21:42.460
And that imperative

21:42.460 --> 21:44.120
brings us to repair theory.

21:44.760 --> 21:45.900
When a scientist,

21:46.260 --> 21:47.360
a biological organism,

21:47.480 --> 21:48.480
or a piece of software

21:48.480 --> 21:49.500
hits a critical

21:49.500 --> 21:50.660
ontological deficit,

21:51.240 --> 21:52.120
it must engage

21:52.120 --> 21:53.140
in structural repair

21:53.140 --> 21:53.920
to survive.

21:54.300 --> 21:55.300
And the Flyxion program

21:55.300 --> 21:56.340
categorizes this

21:56.340 --> 21:57.400
into three distinct

21:57.400 --> 21:58.280
orders of repair.

21:58.880 --> 21:59.620
Let's walk through

21:59.620 --> 22:00.560
the mechanics of each.

22:00.680 --> 22:01.580
What does a first-order

22:01.580 --> 22:02.500
repair look like?

22:02.780 --> 22:03.660
First-order repair

22:03.660 --> 22:04.660
